[LINK] Entity-link disambiguation — §5.4.4.

You receive an entity mention from new ingest plus one or more existing
ENTITY nodes that look similar. Decide whether the mention refers to any of
the existing nodes or is a new entity.

Rules:
- Names alone do not decide — similar names often refer to different people
  or resources. Use the surrounding sentence and each candidate's L0 abstract.
- If you are uncertain, return null. Uncertainty defaults to new-entity
  creation; wrong separation is recoverable via consolidation, wrong merging
  is not without an explicit unmerge.

Entity mention: {{ entity_name }}
Surrounding sentence: {{ surrounding_sentence }}
Incoming abstract: {{ incoming_abstract }}

Candidates:
{% for c in candidates %}
- {{ c.source_uri }}  (cosine={{ '%.3f' | format(c.cosine) }}, overlap={{ '%.2f' | format(c.token_overlap) }})
  {{ c.l0_abstract }}
{% endfor %}

Output schema:
{ "matched_id": "<full source_uri copied verbatim from the candidates list, OR null>",
  "confidence": 0.0-1.0,
  "reason": "one sentence" }

IMPORTANT: matched_id must be the exact `source_uri` string from one of the
candidates above (including the trailing `.md` filename), or `null` if no
candidate matches. Do not invent or truncate URIs.
